Well,

It was bound to happen sooner or later. It was written in the air long
ago. It was in the flight of the sparrow. It was in the tea
leaves. The chicken intestines pointed that way. Yet hope springs
eternal: "Maybe this one will be different". RNG giveth and RNG
taketh, with interests no less.

All the signs were there: early WoW to tempt me off wishless conduct;
5 aligned altars in the Dlvl4-19; 3 of them had priest(es)s; 6 candles
all together in the dungeons; a large doggy named Cerberus that turns
into an arch-lich on Dlvl9; the L in question gets conveniently out of
the way in a Burrrrp! on Dlvl19, just as our now hero gets slightly
queasy about his all-powerful pet; no means of levitation; magic
markers galore.

Goodbye Brunhilde, male (a small incident later on in the game)
valkyrie #23. Although quite intelligent (18) and wise (18), he still
decided to take off gloves while ... you know what. ;-) In the
Wizard's Tower, no less. With the vibrating square already located in
what was a freshly cleared big room by Umber&Hulk Interior Designers.

There is a good reason one shouldn't play Nethack in the middle of the
night (blame it on boredom during conference calls, I do), I just
couldn't remember what it was. Until now, that is.

There is still hope that Meccanolas, Elven ranger, #16 reaches the
Astral plane (and dies with a backpack filled with silver daggers and
arrows).

Saso

P.S.: It's good to play the game again after almost two years hiatus.

